      "title": "Change of occupation and misstatement of age",
      "narration": "Optional provisions may be included at the insurer’s choice. Under change of occupation, if Rosa moves from office estimating to climbing poles, a more hazardous job, benefits are reduced to what her premium would have bought at the new occupation’s rate. If she moves to a less hazardous job, premium drops and the excess is refunded from the date of change. Under misstatement of age, if she gave the wrong birth date, benefits are adjusted to what the premium would have purchased at her true age. Neither provision voids the policy; both correct the bargain.",
