      "title": "Free look, insuring clause and consideration",
      "narration": "Three general provisions frame every policy. The right to examine, or free look, lets the insured return the policy within a stated period after delivery, typically ten days for individual health policies and thirty days for Medicare supplement and long-term care policies in Maryland, for a full refund. The insuring clause is the insurer’s core promise: who is covered, against which perils, for what benefits. The consideration clause states what the insured gives: the premium and the statements in the application. Together they define the exchange, and the rest of the policy qualifies it.",
