      "title": "Interest and military suspension",
      "narration": "Two smaller provisions finish the set. Interest on claim proceeds requires the insurer to pay interest when a claim is paid late; Maryland’s prompt payment law sets the rate, starting at 1.5 percent a month on clean claims unpaid after thirty days. The military suspension provision lets an insured called to active duty suspend the policy, with premium refunded for the suspension period, and reinstate it without evidence of insurability within a set time after discharge. Rosa should know that a noncancelable policy she buys today protects both her coverage and her price, while a guaranteed renewable medical plan protects only the coverage.",
