      "title": "Why comprehensive medical plans are guaranteed renewable",
      "text": "Federal law requires individual and group comprehensive medical coverage to be guaranteed renewable, with nonrenewal allowed only for nonpayment, fraud, moving out of the service area or the insurer leaving the market. Premiums may still rise by class each year, which is the defining feature of guaranteed renewable coverage.",
      "example": "Marcus’s individual medical plan cannot be canceled because he developed diabetes, but his premium can rise with everyone else’s in his age band and area.",
