      "title": "Noncancelable costs more for a reason",
      "text": "A noncancelable disability policy locks the premium schedule, so the insurer bears the risk that claims run higher than expected. Guaranteed renewable disability coverage costs less because the insurer can adjust class premiums. Producers should present the trade-off plainly.",
      "example": "Rosa pays about 20 percent more for a noncancelable policy whose premium cannot change until age 65.",
